WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.589
The analytical reasoning in this module transfers
across SQL systems but some

00:00:04.616 --> 00:00:10.201
syntax changes PostgreSQL can subtract timestamps
directly

00:00:10.227 --> 00:00:13.937
in ways that other databases may express with
functions such as DATEDIFF

00:00:15.687 --> 00:00:20.423
PostgreSQL FILTER is concise for conditional
aggregation while SUM with CASE is

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:26.329
supported more broadly ROLLUP CUBE GROUPING SETS and
window functions

00:00:26.355 --> 00:00:30.895
are widely available in modern databases but exact
syntax and supported options

00:00:30.921 --> 00:00:36.460
can vary When moving a query between systems
preserve the reasoning first

00:00:36.605 --> 00:00:41.157
filter source rows define the grain calculate
measures filter groups and sort

00:00:41.184 --> 00:00:48.048
the report Then adapt the engine-specific syntax
That

00:00:48.061 --> 00:00:52.127
approach is much safer than copying a PostgreSQL
query and assuming every

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.640
database interprets it exactly the same way
